# privacy guard — raw data and real-name keys never enter git
data/
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.parquet
*.local.md
.env
.env.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Anywhere a run's output might get redirected by hand. The validation report and the
# sniff summary quote real tier labels and real event counts.
reports/

# Phase results.
#   results/            REAL-data output: real prices, real margins, real event counts.
#                       Stays local until the pre-publication Fable gate (DECISIONS.md)
#                       clears it for the public repo. Ignored on purpose, for now.
#   results/synthetic/  output of src/pricing/synthetic.py. Nothing in it is real —
#                       Brand A/B, V1..V4, FAKE ids — so it is committable and un-ignored.
# `results/*` (not `results/`) so git still descends into the directory and can see the
# negation below; a plain `results/` would ignore the whole tree and `!` would never fire.
results/*
!results/synthetic/

# Note: the *.csv / *.xls[x] / *.parquet globs above are repo-wide and deliberate.
# Test fixtures are therefore built in Python (tests/synthetic.py), never committed as
# data files — nothing that looks like an export can slip into git by accident.
